  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that levocabastine interacts with DNA polymerase iota, which is a target of multiple compounds, including methyl (7R)-3-hydroxy-7-prop-1-en-2-yl-5,6,7,8-tetrahydronaphthalene-1-carboxylate, (9R,10R)-9,10-Dihydroxy-4,6-heptadecadiyn-3-one, and Neocaesalpin G. All these compounds are known to target DNA polymerase iota, and each of them has a known target LAMA-84. This indicates a potential pathway where levocabastine, through its interaction with DNA polymerase iota, may influence the activity of LAMA-84. The shared target of multiple compounds with LAMA-84 suggests a possible mechanism of action involving DNA polymerase iota, possibly through a common pathway or a direct interaction. The evidence supports a relationship between levocabastine and LAMA-84, mediated through DNA polymerase iota, and highlights the importance of this enzyme in the biological process.",
